Illustrations

A is tried for the murder of B by beating him with a club
with the intention of causing his death.
At A's trial the following facts are in issue:-
A's beating B with the club;
A's causing B's death by such beating;
A's intention to cause B's death.

The question is whether A murdered B. Marks on the
ground, produced by a struggle at or near the place
where the murder was committed, are relevant facts;

